<title>USA: Pacific Telesis oper shr rises to $0.67.</title>
<headline>Pacific Telesis oper shr rises to $0.67.</headline>
<dateline>WARRENTON, Ore. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			 1995</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $0.67		    $0.64</p>
<p> Oper net		 286,000		  275,000</p>
<p> Revs		   2,418,000		2,275,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 428,362		  427,421</p>
<p>					 9  MONTHS</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $2.02		    $1.92</p>
<p> Oper net		 865,000		  817,000</p>
<p> Revs		   7,145,000		6,760,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 428,411		  425,184</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q3 and 9 mos 1995 figures exclude a $3.36 million extraordinary loss due to accounting changes. The loss reduced Q3 earnings by $7.86 a share and 9 mos by $7.90 a share. After adjusting for the changes, Q3 net loss was $7.22 a share and 9 mos net loss was $5.98 a share.</p>
<p>Full name is Pacific Telesis Group.</p>
<p>First Call Q3 mean estimate is $0.67 a share.</p>
</text>
